📗 📟 What a connection needs to know about the server around it. 📗
🐊 📟 🍇
  📗 Whether the server has been asked to stop. 📗
  ❗️ 🛑 ➡️ 👌

  📗
    Whether a stop has been asked for that has not taken hold yet: the server
    still answers, for as long as server.shutdownDelayMs says, and from now on
    no connection is kept, so that whoever sends the requests comes back on a
    new one while there is still someone to take it.
  📗
  ❗️ 🔔 ➡️ 👌

  📗 Whether every worker is busy while a client waits to be accepted. 📗
  ❗️ 🥵 ➡️ 👌

  📗 Called for each request the server core refuses before it reaches any middleware. 📗
  ❗️ 📝 status 🔢 reason 🔡

  📗
    Called with 1 when a request starts to arrive on a connection, and with -1
    when that request has been answered or given up. What is counted is work
    that a stop should wait for; a connection that is merely open is not.
  📗
  ❗️ 💼 change 🔢
